{
  "id": "Compound::DB00383 - Gene::1131",
  "verbalization": "Oxyphencyclimine is likely to interact with Chrm3 through a mechanism involving the G-protein coupled receptor system. The evidence suggests that Oxyphencyclimine binds to Chrm2, which is involved in the activation of G-protein coupled receptors, and that Chrm2 participates in activities related to acetylcholine receptors, including Muscarinic and Neurotransmitter receptor functions. These pathways ultimately lead to Chrm3 being part of the receptor complex. The overlapping roles of Chrm2 in different receptor activities imply a shared functional context, suggesting that Oxyphencyclimine may modulate Chrm3 through a common intermediary. The consistent binding to Chrm2 and the involvement of G-protein coupled receptor activities across different paths support a unified mechanism, where Oxyphencyclimine influences Chrm3 via a pathway involving G-protein coupled acetylcholine or neurotransmitter receptors.",
